[4] {'uid': 'c8ccbc9a-1b2e-4fa2-84f2-aa26e91bc2bb', 'order': 5, 'text': 'HC2’s accrual for cash and equity-based bonus arrangements of HC2 executive employees as of December 31, 2019 and 2018 resulted in a $4.4 million decrease in expense recognized. These changes reflect the underlying performance in the Compensation NAV in the respective periods. In 2019 the NAV did not meet the hurdle rate, while in 2018 it grew approximately 21%.'}
[5] {'uid': 'bb3548a0-adaa-46c7-bae4-4bd921e48ff0', 'order': 6, 'text': 'For 2019, Compensation NAV did not meet the hurdle rate, and declined by 26.1%, resulting primarily from external events that occurred in the fourth quarter at our Insurance segment, with respect to our views on the future of the management fee agreement, along with our expectations of future dividends, after recent and ongoing discussions with our domestic regulator.'}
